  },
  "content": {
    "paragraphs": [
      {
        "id": "p1",
        "order": 1,
        "sentences": [
          {
            "id": "s1",
            "text": "Often called “a love poem in stone,” the Taj Mahal is one of the most beautiful buildings ever made."
          },
          {
            "id": "s2",
            "text": "It is also perhaps the most beautiful expression of love in the world."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p2",
        "order": 2,
        "sentences": [
          {
            "id": "s3",
            "text": "The emperor Shah Jahan built the Taj Mahal for his empress, Mumtaz Mahal."
          },
          {
            "id": "s4",
            "text": "They lived happily together for 18 years."
          },
          {
            "id": "s5",
            "text": "Then, in 1631, Mumtaz died during the birth of their fourteenth child."
          },
          {
            "id": "s6",
            "text": "Before she died, the emperor made her a promise."
          },
          {
            "id": "s7",
            "text": "To remember her, he would build the most beautiful monument in the world."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p3",
        "order": 3,
        "sentences": [
          {
            "id": "s8",
            "text": "Why did the emperor build the Taj Mahal?"
          },
          {
            "id": "s9",
            "text": "Is it easy to build the Taj Mahal? Why? Why do you think Shah Jahan’s son put him in prison?"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p4",
        "order": 4,
        "sentences": [
          {
            "id": "s10",
            "text": "Building the Taj Mahal was a huge task."
          },
          {
            "id": "s11",
            "text": "It is said that it took more than 20,000 people and 1,000 elephants."
          },
          {
            "id": "s12",
            "text": "They worked for over 20 years to build the monument and its central dome."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p5",
        "order": 5,
        "sentences": [
          {
            "id": "s13",
            "text": "In 1658, five years after the building was finished, Shah Jahan’s son became emperor."
          },
          {
            "id": "s14",
            "text": "He put Shah Jahan in prison. 4 Shah Jahan stayed there until his death in 1666."
          },
          {
            "id": "s15",
            "text": "His body was then put in the Taj Mahal with the woman he loved."
          },
          {
            "id": "s16",
            "text": "it took him 20 years to complete the task."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p6",
        "order": 6,
        "sentences": [
          {
            "id": "s17",
            "text": "What probably happened to the builder? Why? Why do tourists like to visit Taj Mahal?"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p7",
        "order": 7,
        "sentences": [
          {
            "id": "s18",
            "text": "There are many legends about the Taj Mahal."
          },
          {
            "id": "s19",
            "text": "In one story, Shah Jahan had the builders’ hands cut off after the building was complete."
          },
          {
            "id": "s20",
            "text": "This was supposedly done so they could never build anything as beautiful as the Taj Mahal."
          },
          {
            "id": "s21",
            "text": "Another says he also wanted to build a black Taj Mahal."
          },
          {
            "id": "s22",
            "text": "These are interesting stories, but they are probably not true."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p8",
        "order": 8,
        "sentences": [
          {
            "id": "s23",
            "text": "The love story between Shah Jahan and his wife ended sadly."
          },
          {
            "id": "s24",
            "text": "But the monument to their love still stands today."
          },
          {
            "id": "s25",
            "text": "Millions of tourists visit every year."
          },
          {
            "id": "s26",
            "text": "They come to see the marble change color in the light of the rising sun or a full moon."
          },
          {
            "id": "s27",
            "text": "have sth. done I hadafter."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
